{
  "$comment": [
    "AUTHORED DATA, not derived. Read by tools/build-content.ts (feature 020).",
    "",
    "What a power does ON ARRIVAL. The workbook has no rider column, and `Power`",
    "had no rider field at all until 020 -- so a rider was UNREPRESENTABLE rather",
    "than merely unauthored, which is why resolve.ts could honestly hardcode",
    "`ridersLanded: []` at every exit.",
    "",
    "NO MAGNITUDES AND NO DURATIONS LIVE HERE. Both derive from the applying",
    "power's tier via the table in resources/mechanics/05-status.md, so a rebalance",
    "edits one table instead of 87 entries (Constitution XV). The schema is strict",
    "and rejects a magnitude by name. The single exception is `band` for shred,",
    "whose 20/30/40% is the one magnitude the tier table does not determine.",
    "",
    "ORDER IS SIGNIFICANT. Riders are contested one RNG draw each, in the order",
    "written here, and the draw order is part of the engine contract. This is an",
    "array for that reason and never an object.",
    "",
    "EVERY ACTIVE POWER APPEARS, including those with none. An empty list means",
    "\"deliberately carries no rider\"; being absent is a build failure. Without that",
    "distinction \"has none\" and \"nobody has read this prompt yet\" look identical,",
    "which is the exact collapse FR-018 exists to prevent.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED BY READING ALL 87 PROMPTS, ONE AT A TIME. Not extracted. The explicit",
    "\"Rider:\" clause is a tier-1/tier-2 convention only -- 18 powers carry it, the",
    "tier-0 autos state they have NONE, and every tier-3/4/5 power folds its effect",
    "into prose (\"Coll also gains a temporary Magic Resist buff\"). A regex over the",
    "Prompt column returns zero riders for the entire top half of the roster and",
    "looks like a clean answer.",
    "",
    "`at` IS NOT `friendly`. Most buffs in this roster ride an ATTACK and land on",
    "the caster; the power still aims at an enemy. See the same warning in",
    "tools/power-targeting.json, which learned it first.",
    "",
    "$damageShape and $unmodelled below are documentation, not data. The first",
    "records powers whose special behaviour is a damage modifier rather than a",
    "status, so an empty list is never mistaken for an unread prompt. The second",
    "records effects the prompts describe that 05-status.md has no family for --",
    "adding a seventh family is a design decision, not a build one."
  ],
